From: DuskyProjects <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: gl-be9300: select the USB side of the shared PHY

Describe the IPQ5332 USB/PCIe PHY mux using the register and value from
Qualcomm's downstream IPQ5332 device tree. The DWC3 glue selects this
mux before resetting the controller.

The tcsr syscon starts at 0x01937000, so offset 0x10540 resolves to the
verified physical register 0x01947540.

---
 target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts
@@ -486,6 +486,12 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&usb {
+	qcom,multiplexed-phy;
+	qcom,phy-mux-regs = <&tcsr 0x10540>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &usb_dwc {
 	status = "okay";
 };
